#
# prima-materia — New Thought: Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand
# (1928)
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:NewThought, kept apart from
# traditions/new-thought.ttl, which declares the tradition and its works
# (pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand is declared there, not here). The whole
# book was read, pp. 7-85, in the order of its twenty-nine sections; the nodes
# follow the sections and, within each, the page that carries them. Every
# source names the section title as the contents page gives it.
#
# The printing read is the DeVorss reprint, which calls the author "the late
# Florence Scovel Shinn" and so postdates 1940; its text, pagination and
# contents are those of the 1928 book. Two archive.org scans of this printing
# were read against each other: yourwordisyourwa00flor (2012) for the text and
# yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 (2025, Boston Public Library) for the running heads
# that the first lacks (pp. 15, 17, 19, 21).
#
# Most of the book is affirmations grouped under the thing asked for. Every
# promise an affirmation makes is entered as a capacity with a yielding from
# the section's affirmation practice; where the same promise returns in a later
# section, the capacity is one node and the yielding is added.
#
# Every record of this harvest was compared with the nodes of
# traditions/new-thought-game-of-life.ttl (The Game of Life and How to Play It,
# to which this book calls itself a sequel). Where a node there carries the
# same being, practice or caution, no node is written here and links point at
# it: pmc:NewThoughtShinnInfiniteIntelligence, pmc:NewThoughtShinnChristWithin,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuperconsciousMind, pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineMind,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSubconsciousMind, pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightWork,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnWorldOfTheWondrous, pmc:NewThoughtShinnForceAMentalPicture,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnDiggingDitches, pmp:NewThoughtShinnDenyingLoss,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnLawOfForgiveness and pmp:NewThoughtShinnFollowingAHunch.
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#924 with two independent extraction passes
# over the text, reconciled by page and word overlap, then integrated by a
# reader of the whole text. Identifiers are pmc:NewThoughtShinn or
# pmp:NewThoughtShinn plus the author's own wording in PascalCase. Signs of
# success, conditions of failure and capacities carry a note beginning
# "Counted as". Cases the author tells of clients and others are entered as
# third-party ascriptions, her own as first-person reports.
#

#
# Your Word is Your Wand
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnManSWordIsHisWand a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Man's word is his wand"@en, "Das Wort des Menschen ist sein Zauberstab"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spoken word carries magic and power and can be used like a wand to change conditions."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"Man's word is his wand\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in Matthew 12:37; Proverbs 18:21 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 7; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWavingOverItTheWandOfHisWord a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waving the wand of the word over a condition"@en, "Den Zauberstab des Wortes über eine Lage schwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Speaking the right word over an unhappy condition so that its opposite appears in its place."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"waving over it the wand of his word\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in Matthew 12:37; Proverbs 18:21 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 7; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnChangeAnUnhappyCondition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power to change an unhappy condition"@en, "Macht, eine unglückliche Lage zu wandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through the word man can turn sorrow into joy, sickness into health and lack into plenty."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"power to change an unhappy condition\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 7; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWavingOverItTheWandOfHisWordYieldsChangeAnUnhappyCondition a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Waving the wand of the word over a condition brings power to change an unhappy condition"@en, "Den Zauberstab des Wortes über eine Lage schwingen bewirkt: Macht, eine unglückliche Lage zu wandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds that waving the wand of the word over a condition brings this about: power to change an unhappy condition."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWavingOverItTheWandOfHisWord ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnChangeAnUnhappyCondition ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 7; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnMagicPurseOfTheSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment of the magic purse of the Spirit"@en, "Behandlung mit der Zauberbörse des Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blessing the little money one has and speaking of a purse of the Spirit that can never be depleted and is seen crammed, jammed with money."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the magic purse of the Spirit\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, pp. 7-8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAsMoneyGoesOutMoneyComesIn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Supply that is never depleted"@en, "Versorgung, die nie erschöpft wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "A supply in which, as money goes out, money immediately comes in under grace; reported as a gift of six thousand dollars."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"as money goes out, immediately money comes in\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, pp. 7-8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

