pmc:NewThoughtShinnIFeelMyBagHeavyWithMoney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the bag heavy with money"@en, "Gefühl, dass die Tasche schwer von Geld ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the magic-purse treatment the client reported feeling her bag heavy with money, a sign of faith taking hold."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"I feel my bag heavy with money\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text names it as a mark that the work has taken effect. Counted apart from conditions of failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldThePictureOfPlenty a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding the picture of plenty"@en, "Das Bild der Fülle halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The practitioner keeps the image of abundance for the client and does nothing that would mean seeing lack for her."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"hold the picture of plenty\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIDidNotDareRefuseIt a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not refusing the love offering"@en, "Die Liebesgabe nicht zurückweisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Refusing the client's dollar would have meant seeing lack for her, so the author did not dare refuse it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldThePictureOfPlenty ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"I did not dare refuse it and see lack for her\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

