pmp:NewThoughtShinnKnowTheTruthOfEverySituation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing the Truth of every situation"@en, "Die Wahrheit jeder Lage erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognising that there is no Truth in lack or limitation and speaking the word accordingly over the situation one faces."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"know the Truth of every situation\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in John 8:32 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNoTruthInLackOrLimitation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "There is no Truth in lack or limitation"@en, "In Mangel und Begrenzung ist keine Wahrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lack and limitation have no reality before Truth and yield when the word is spoken over them."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"There is no Truth in lack or limitation\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheTruthShallMakeYouFree a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom through Truth; the wilderness blossoms"@en, "Befreiung durch die Wahrheit; die Wüste blüht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing the Truth frees man from lack; over lack the word makes the wilderness rejoice and blossom as the rose."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the Truth shall make you free\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in John 8:32; Isaiah 35:1 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
