pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearDoubtAnxietyAngerResentment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear, doubt, anxiety, anger, resentment as causes of disease and disaster"@en, "Furcht, Zweifel, Sorge, Zorn, Groll als Ursachen von Krankheit und Unglück"@de ;
    skos:definition "These emotions break down the body's cells, shock the nerves and cause disease and disaster."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the causes of disease and disaster\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappinessAndHealth fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Your Word is Your Wand, p. 8; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnControlBeforeHappinessAndHealth a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Emotional control before happiness and health"@en, "Gefühlsbeherrschung vor Glück und Gesundheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Happiness and health cannot be had without control of the emotions; uncontrolled fear and resentment cause disease and disaster."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappinessAndHealth ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnAbsoluteControlOfTheEmotionalNature ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
