pmc:NewThoughtShinnRelaxesAllNervousTension a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release of nervous tension; being undisturbed by adverse appearances"@en, "Lösen aller Nervenspannung; Unberührtheit von widrigen Anschein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing one is protected, one relaxes, is satisfied and stays undisturbed by adverse appearances."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"he relaxes all nervous tension\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in Isaiah 43:19 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Happiness, p. 23; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPerfectFaithInGodYieldsRelaxesAllNervousTension a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Perfect faith in God; knowing an invincible power protects brings release of nervous tension; being undisturbed by adverse appearances"@en, "Vollkommener Glaube an Gott; wissen, dass eine unbesiegbare Macht schützt bewirkt: Lösen aller Nervenspannung; Unberührtheit von widrigen Anschein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds that perfect faith in God; knowing an invincible power protects brings this about: release of nervous tension; being undisturbed by adverse appearances."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnPerfectFaithInGod ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRelaxesAllNervousTension ;
    skos:note "Grounded in Isaiah 43:19 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Happiness, p. 23; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAngerResentmentIllWillJealousyRevenge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anger, resentment, ill-will, jealousy and revenge rob happiness"@en, "Zorn, Groll, Missgunst, Eifersucht und Rache rauben das Glück"@de ;
    skos:definition "These emotions take away happiness and bring sickness, failure and poverty in their wake."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"rob man of his happiness\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappiness fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Happiness, p. 23; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnUndisturbedByAdverseAppearances a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Undisturbed by adverse appearances"@en, "Unbeirrt von widrigem Anschein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remaining unmoved by appearances, knowing Infinite Intelligence uses every situation to bring one's good."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"undisturbed by adverse appearances\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
