#
# Love
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWithLoveUsuallyComesTerrificFear a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of 'the other woman' brings interference"@en, "Furcht vor 'der anderen Frau' zieht Störung an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Belief in duality makes a woman fear a rival; as long as she visualizes interference, it will come."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"So long as she visualizes interference, it will come\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnBeingLovedByTheManSheLoves fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Love, p. 27; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOnlyOneness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "In reality there is only oneness"@en, "In Wirklichkeit gibt es nur Einheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Duality is a false belief; in truth there is only oneness, so no rival can intervene."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"in reality there is only oneness\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Love, p. 27; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

