#
# Loss
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBeliefOfLoss a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Loss shows a belief of loss in the subconscious"@en, "Verlust zeigt einen Verlustglauben im Unterbewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Losing something reveals a false belief of loss; erase the belief and the article or its equivalent appears."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"a belief of loss in his subconscious mind\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Loss, p. 46; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBeliefOfLossInSubconscious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A belief of loss as cause of losing"@en, "Ein Verlustglaube als Ursache des Verlierens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The belief of loss in the subconscious is what makes one lose things."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"a belief of loss\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnItOrItsEquivalent fails."@en ;
