#
# Debt
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBeliefOfDebt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Debt shows a belief of debt in the subconscious"@en, "Schulden zeigen einen Schuldenglauben im Unterbewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Owing or being owed money reveals a belief of debt that must be neutralized for conditions to change."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"a belief of debt\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Debt, p. 48; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBeliefOfDebtInSubconscious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A belief of debt as cause of unpaid debt"@en, "Ein Schuldenglaube als Ursache unbezahlter Schulden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The belief of debt in the subconscious keeps the debt in place."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"a belief of debt\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnAllIsSquared fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Debt, p. 48; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWorkOnYourselfNotTheMan a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working on oneself, not on the debtor"@en, "An sich selbst arbeiten, nicht am Schuldner"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changing one's own belief instead of trying to compel the other person."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"You must work on yourself, not the man\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
