#
# Sales
#

pmp:NewThoughtShinnAskedGodToSell a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking God to sell to the right person for the right price, unmindful of appearances"@en, "Gott bitten, an die rechte Person zum rechten Preis zu verkaufen, ohne auf den Anschein zu achten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Placing the sale with God, ignoring discouraging appearances, and preparing for it (polishing the furniture)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"asked God to sell her furniture\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Sales, p. 50; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSoldWithoutAnyCommission a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Selling property under grace"@en, "Verkauf von Eigentum unter Gnade"@de ;
    skos:definition "Goods and property sold despite adverse conditions, reported as furniture and house sold in a blizzard without an agent."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"all the furniture was sold\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
