pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhenManIsHarmoniousAndHappyHeIsHealthy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When man is harmonious and happy he is healthy"@en, "Wer harmonisch und glücklich ist, ist gesund"@de ;
    skos:definition "Health follows harmony and happiness."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"harmonious and happy\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Health, p. 61; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAllSicknessComesFromSin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sickness comes from sin or violation of Spiritual Law"@en, "Krankheit kommt aus Sünde oder Verletzung des geistigen Gesetzes"@de ;
    skos:definition "All sickness is caused by sin, understood as violating Spiritual Law."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"violation of Spiritual Law\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in Matthew 9:2-6 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRadiantHealth fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Health, p. 61; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTearDownTheCellsOfTheBody a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resentment, ill-will, hate and fear tear down the body"@en, "Groll, Missgunst, Hass und Furcht zerstören den Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "These emotions break down the body's cells and poison the blood."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"tear down the cells of the body and poison the blood\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRadiantHealth fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Health, p. 61; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHoldingWrongMentalPictures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wrong mental pictures cause accidents, old age and death"@en, "Falsche innere Bilder verursachen Unfälle, Alter und Tod"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accidents, ageing and death itself come from holding wrong mental pictures."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"holding wrong mental pictures\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnTimelessBirthlessAndDeathless fails."@en ;
