#
# Eyes
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCorrespondences a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mental correspondences of bodily ailments"@en, "Seelische Entsprechungen körperlicher Leiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the Health sections the author assigns to each ailment a 'Correspondence', a mental or emotional cause, before giving its affirmation."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Florence Scovel Shinn, in Your Word Is Your Wand" ;
    dcterms:date "1928"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "The scheme as the author states it: Each ailment has its correspondence: imperfect vision - fear, suspicion, seeing obstacles, not living in the now; anaemia - unfed desires; deafness - strong personal will; rheumatism - faultfinding; false growths - jealousy, hatred, resentment, fear; heart disease - fear, anger."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"Correspondence\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Eyes, pp. 63-69; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImperfectVisionCorrespondence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Correspondence of imperfect vision"@en, "Entsprechung von Sehschwäche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imperfect vision corresponds to fear, suspicion, seeing obstacles, watching for unhappy events and not living in the now."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"Correspondences\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnPerfectSight fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Eyes, p. 63; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

