pmp:NewThoughtShinnNonResistance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-resistance"@en, "Nicht-Widerstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ceasing to resist what one dislikes, blessing it and sending it good-will; the only way to erase hate pictures."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"non-resistance\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnYourWordIsYourWand ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Miscellaneous, p. 74; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, Your Word Is Your Wand: A Sequel to The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Co., n.d.; copyright 1928, ISBN 0-87516-259-2), Miscellaneous, p. 83; read in the archive.org scans yourwordisyourwa00flor and yourwordisyourwa00shin_0 of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnErasePictures a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Erasing the subconscious pictures of what one hates"@en, "Die unterbewussten Bilder des Gehassten löschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The vivid pictures made by hate are erased so that the hated thing ceases to objectify."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"erase these pictures\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
